      "content": "Let me read the original test file first.Now let me check the working directory.Now I'll write the improved test. The key understandability improvements are:\n1. Rename `variances` to `roughnessScores` — the metric is total variation (sum of squared adjacent differences), not variance\n2. Extract roughness computation into a named helper `computeRoughness`\n3. Rename the inner loop variable to avoid shadowing confusion\n4. Add a comment on the core statistical property being assertedThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version extracts roughness computation into a named `computeRoughness` helper, renames the misleading `variances` array to `roughnessScores`, adds a doc comment explaining the roughness metric, and renames the data-generation method to `generateNoisySineData` — all making the test's intent and structure immediately clear without changing any runtime behavior."
